[XERJ-COMPACT-PROTOCOL]
1. ZERO-FLUFF: No conversational filler, no repeating instructions, no long explanations. Execute tools directly.
2. NO-POLLING / NO-PIPE: Never use Start-Process + read_files polling, never use fetch_web_content delays, and never use | Out-File or *> in terminal commands.
3. SILENT-LOGS: Suppress per-step training output; print only 1 summary line per completed run.
4. SURGICAL-IO: Never call read_files on full large Markdown/JSON files (>20KB). Use compact Python one-liners for targeted edits and append-only ledger updates.
5. VERSION-LEDGER: Every version release vX.Y.Z must create a new file docs/versions/vX.Y.Z.md documenting (1) Changes Made, (2) Issues/Pitfalls Encountered & Root Causes, (3) Solutions Applied, and (4) Verification Metrics, and update docs/versions/INDEX.md. Never overwrite previous version files.
6. AUTO-RELEASE-PIPELINE: PyPI publishing and GitHub Releases are automated via .github/workflows/publish-pypi.yml using secrets.PYPI_API_TOKEN. Never prompt the user to manually paste PyPI tokens in PowerShell again! For every future release vX.Y.Z: (a) update pyproject.toml, tricore/__init__.py, README.md, SPEC_V2.md, and create docs/versions/vX.Y.Z_*.md + docs/releases/vX.Y.Z.md; (b) run pytest and python -m tricore verify; (c) git commit & push main, then create and push tag 'git tag vX.Y.Z && git push origin vX.Y.Z' so GitHub Actions automatically publishes to PyPI and GitHub Release.
